WEBVTT

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:14.570
<i>Kakugane, the paranormal alloy forged</i> <i>from the essence of alchemy...</i>

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.810
<i>Activated by the person's fighting instinct,</i>

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.220
<i>the possessor converts</i> <i>their latent power into form</i>

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.250
<i>and creates a weapon like no other.</i>

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.190
<i>That is Buso Renkin.</i>

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.110
The all-out attack on Victor has begun.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:44.220
The Alchemist Warriors each makes full use of their Buso Renkin to corner Victor.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.260
But Victor evolves into his third stage,

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.100
showing the Alchemist Army the extent of his true powers.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.170
Meanwhile, Kazuki and the others arrive at Newton Apple Girls' Academy

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.900
and come upon the white kakugane

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.470
that could restore Kazuki to human form.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.410
However...!

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:20.830
<i>lt will be a few more days before</i> <i>the white kakugane is complete.</i>

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.700
"There are two Victors, and only one white kakugane!"

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.030
Think it over carefully before you make your decision.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.860
"Only one of the two,
Victor or Kazuki Muto..."

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.270
This must be quite a shock for you to handle.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.070
But you are still fortunate that you have a choice.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.180
"Can be restored back to human!"

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.600
Aw man... l hate going to summer school.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.870
lt's supposed to be vacation!

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:11.370
Huh?!

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.370
Oh, they're finally here.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.910
The first bell has already rung.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.310
Aren't you guys even going to try to hurry?

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.420
Hey! Long time no see!

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.340
Good grief!

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.550
—Kazuki! Tokiko!
—Kazuki! Tokiko!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.360
lf we don't hurry, we'll be late for homeroom!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.090
So, how did it go?

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.860
Have things progressed a bit between the two of you?

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.900
Huh? What do you mean?

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.730
lsn't it about time you made it clear to her? l'm sure Tokiko would feel more...

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.000
H-Hey...

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.500
Stay still!

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:44.740
I'll splatter your guts!

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:50.880
Spirited, aren't they?

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.240
They're in top form!

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.950
You would think they didn't have a worry in the world!

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.250
What's there to think about!
Kazuki has done nothing wrong.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.730
He should just return himself to human form with dignity.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.360
You're right. Not only has he done nothing wrong,

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.560
he has protected this school and this city over and over again...

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.430
But...

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.270
lt is for that very reason, because of the kind of boy he is,

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.980
that he cannot just leave Victor like that.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:21.210
He...is truly a strong boy.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.820
Yes. lt is as if he were born to become a warrior.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.420
From here on out,

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.180
he will become stronger and stronger in both mind and body.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.050
But...

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.220
ln spite of that, he is still only a 17-year-old high school kid!

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.570
lt's true! You have returned!
Welcome back!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.040
Oh! Mahiro, l'm back!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.040
Tokiko!

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.050
Oh, you too Kazuki, welcome back!

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.180
Yeah.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:03:59.450
Now, now!

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.220
She may not look it, but she was really worried about you!

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:02.910
So?!

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.920
You came back in one piece,

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.430
so that means your mission has been completed without any incident, right?

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:08.090
Yes!

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.200
ln that case, we only have a half day today,

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.360
so how about we all hang out after this!

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.840
Nice idea!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.530
Kazuki, you and Tokiko can come too, can't you?

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.110
Of course.
So, where do we want to go?

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.940
l want to go to an amusement park!

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.810
That's a good idea!
An amusement park!

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.110
What about the pool?

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.320
That might be good, too!

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.890
But, the pools in town won't have girls wearing their school swimsuits!

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.290
K-Kazuki!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.560
Something like bowling might be good, as well.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.950
How about a go-playing parlor?

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.520
Uh-uh. An amusement park would be best, after all.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:43.350
You must really love the amusement park, don't you?

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.430
As a matter of fact, l'm crazy about them too!

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.970
What's the meaning of this?!

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.640
The matter is clear-cut.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.670
After we topple Victor, with whom we are now battling,

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.510
the re-extermination of Kazuki Muto awaits us.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.040
That's all there is to it.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.440
Let go of me!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.750
Warrior Chief Hiwatari!

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:12.860
What is it?

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.320
The 7th and 8th units have almost completely been wiped out!

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.900
An order has been issued

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:20.870
to disband the second-class combat deployment immediately

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.900
and revert to backing up Buster Baron with a wave of attacks.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.300
All right! lt's your turn now!

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.570
Fall in!

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.410
Busujima, you return to headquarters first...

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:32.070
Hold it!

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:36.380
Do you mean to say that you'll use Muto to defeat Victor,

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.510
but when you're finished, you'll just kill him again?!

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.390
Well, in this case, what would you do?

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.450
Just think.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:45.090
What good is your grumbling going to do? Nothing.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:49.390
Our reality at present is merely to kill the enemy in front of our eyes.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:51.850
Am l mistaken?

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.600
Well, ultimately, it doesn't matter which we take care of first.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.800
lf we had killed that brat when we had the chance,

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.140
things wouldn't have gotten this complicated!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.110
Absurd, isn't it?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.080
The world we live in...

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:10.840
l understand.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.710
l too, shall concentrate on the enemy before my eyes for now.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.760
But l will think over my actions when the time comes.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.820
That is a positive and constructive opinion.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:21.160
Here you go.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.760
<i>Muto... l will never give up!</i>

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:44.110
Tokiko, we're going on ahead, so won't you please wait for Kazuki?

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.310
We'll be waiting at the station...

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.510
Huh? l don't mind,

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:50.450
but wouldn't it be better if we just all go together?

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.560
Okay, we're counting on you!

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:53.720
See you later!

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:54.820
Oh, hey!

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:55.860
Wait a minute!

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.840
<i>You came back in one piece,</i>

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.380
<i>so that means your mission has been</i> <i>completed without any incident, right?</i>

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:12.140
<i>Yes!</i>

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.010
l lied to them...

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:21.620
lsn't it better than making them worry unnecessarily?

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:22.950
Gota?

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:27.080
l was worried that perhaps Tokiko was being treated like an outcast at school,

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:30.320
but your younger sister and your friends are good people.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:41.970
Whatever choice you make, l will do anything l can to aid you

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.710
as long as you vow not to make Tokiko suffer.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.510
As long as what we want to protect is the same,

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.180
then we are comrades!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.350
Gota!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.220
l won't shake your hand, though.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.720
You and l may be comrades,

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.050
but we are still rivals in love!

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.940
What makes that girl so great?

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.100
lt goes beyond comprehension and almost that of a fantasy.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:14.800
Chono!

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:15.600
Hey...

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:20.010
You. Here l thought you haven't shown yourself after Newton Apple...

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.780
Where on earth have you been?

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:26.990
ln my secret lab, of course, conducting research on the white kakugane!

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.190
You're...planning to make another white kakugane?!

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.390
My ultimate goal is for me, the ultimate super-being,

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.790
to defeat the human Kazuki Muto!

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.390
And for that to happen,

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.230
it is essential to have the white kakugane!

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.630
But Alexandria said...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.490
<i>How long would it take from now</i>

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:48.870
<i>to start refining a black kakugane</i> <i>from scratch and create another one?</i>

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:54.540
<i>The process for refining the black kakugane</i> <i>was lost 100 years ago.</i>

00:08:55.150 --> 00:09:01.520
<i>lt would be almost impossible</i> <i>to duplicate one from my aged brain.</i>

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.350
Humph! When l was a human being,

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.860
all of the doctors told me that my days were numbered!

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.990
As you can see, l am still alive and kicking!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.300
Choices are not something given to you by others.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:17.390
You create them by yourself!

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.440
Muto, whichever decision you make...

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.480
l am not giving up on settling our score!

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.740
Yeah, l know!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.620
Tokiko, sorry to have kept you waiting!

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.780
What took you so long?

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:35.850
Did something happen?!

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.850
Huh? No, nothing.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.460
Say, where is everyone?

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:40.920
They went on ahead.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.860
lf we hurry, we'll be able to catch right up with them...

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.960
Oh, really?
Well, shall we get going?

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.730
lt's hot, isn't it?

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.770
Hm? Oh yes...

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:56.870
Kazuki...

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:01.350
Are you going to be all right?
At a time like this?

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.050
l'm all right.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:06.190
Okay. lf you say so.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.380
Yeah. Thank you!

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:10.510
Come on!

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:24.540
The sky is a deep blue, isn't it?

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.170
Yeah. Sure is hotter than usual this year.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:40.390
Thank you for waiting.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:43.960
Here you are, Tokiko.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.350
Um... thank you.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:55.530
What is it?

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:56.630
When we were little,

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:00.640
Mahiro and l used to eat snow cones in the summer.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.710
l was a boy, so l would order melon-flavored syrup,

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.680
and Mahiro was a girl, so she would get the strawberry flavor.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.710
But Mahiro would want to try the melon flavor,

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:12.410
so l gave her some, but it spilled on her dress...

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.420
And then she started to cry,

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.480
and l got flustered and tried to console her.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:21.220
But by the time she stopped crying, our shaved ice had all melted away.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.660
So, you and your sister have gotten along well together since way back when.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:27.630
Yup!

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:36.440
lt's my first time to hear about your childhood.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.270
Really?

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:42.310
l find it rather refreshing to hear people tell such stories.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.980
Perhaps because all l have is the present.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:46.420
What do you mean?

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.150
l have no past.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.990
The doctor told me

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.720
that it seems to be partial memory impairment due to trauma.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.360
Because of that, my memories of the past are quite vague.

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:02.000
But, let's not talk about me now.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.990
Anyway, that's just the way it is...

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:05.470
l wonder if that's really true.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:07.240
The present isn't all you have.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:09.270
You cannot reconstruct the past, but...

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:12.540
l would like to see the future together with you, Tokiko.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:19.480
Yes, you're right. l would like to see the future with you too.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:21.780
Are you embarrassed?

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:24.320
Shut up!
Don't say things like that!

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.860
—Ouch, ouch, ouch!
—Oww! Brain freeze!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.630
Oh, here you are!

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:36.160
What are you doing in such a place?!

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.900
l was worried the two of you would run off into the sunset.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.570
lsn't that expression a little outdated?

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:41.900
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.570
We were just loitering around a bit.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.240
But, how nice!
Snow cones!

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:47.570
Let's have some before we go!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:50.050
No, we should hurry to the amusement park!

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.210
Are you that fond of amusement parks?!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.810
lt just means that he still has the heart of a child...

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.060
Mommy!

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:19.570
Around and around it goes.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.340
Haunted House

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:31.860
Yeah yeah...

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.820
Okakura!

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:49.470
Are you all right? Okakura!

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:51.440
For someone who loves amusement parks,

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.840
you're surprisingly weak-hearted.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.040
Let's ride that one next!

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.280
Let's go, Tokiko!

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.550
No, l think I'll skip this one.
I'll rest for a bit.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.320
Oh, okay...
Well, let's go, Okakura!

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.030
Rokumasu, Daihama!

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.430
—Okay!
—Yeah!

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:14.130
No--!

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.000
O-Okakura?!

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:43.660
All right!

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.860
Let's ride on the Flying Carpet next!

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:49.300
Do l have to?

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.700
Ah! Wait a minute!

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.270
Are we still going?

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:55.430
Come on, come on!

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.180
Come on Tokiko, you're coming too!

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.140
Hm? Uh, right...

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:25.710
Ah, here she comes.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:28.430
Sorry.
Well, shall we be getting back?

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.600
Uh-huh, there's going to be a post-party party!

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:31.510
Let's go do karaoke!

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:32.780
Karaoke?!

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:33.570
Yeah!

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:37.710
I'll let you hear some of my hot rock 'n' roll.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.510
l've come prepared with earplugs.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:41.750
Why are you carrying something like that?

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:42.620
Forget that!

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:44.320
The question is, why would you put earplugs in when l'm singing?

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:49.920
Sorry, l think I'll go back a little early.

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.360
Really?

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.690
Are you tired out?

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:53.790
Are you feeling okay?

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:54.530
Yeah!

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.130
That's probably a wise decision...

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.840
What do you mean by that?!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.410
ln that case...

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:02.740
Tokiko, you're coming with us, aren't you?

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.240
You mustn't leave yet!

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:08.880
See you later, Kazuki.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.240
Take it easy man!

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:11.550
Be careful!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.050
Don't catch cold!

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:14.850
Right...

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.520
See you guys!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:50.650
<i>How you use this...will be</i> <i>your decision Kazuki.</i>

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:57.090
<i>Whatever choice you make,</i> <i>l will do anything l can to aid you</i>

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.630
<i>as long as you vow not</i> <i>to make Tokiko suffer.</i>

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.500
<i>Muto, whichever decision you make,</i>

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:06.370
<i>l am not giving up on settling our score!</i>

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:09.060
<i>The truth is, l've already decided.</i>

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:11.640
<i>l know that.</i>

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:24.350
<i>But if l do that, I'll...</i>

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.150
<i>l will protect everyone...</i>

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.460
<i>but will somebody please protect me?!</i>

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.360
Are you all right?

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:40.700
Tokiko, what are you doing here?

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:43.330
This is my special place...

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.070
Oh, that's right...

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.610
lt's not like you to leave early.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.750
Everyone was worried about you.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.250
Yeah.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:01.920
Oh yeah, Kazuki...

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.060
Look. Over there.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.230
The haunted factory behind the school...

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:16.210
You tried to protect me that time.

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:18.370
Thank you.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:22.980
<i>Oh that's right...</i>

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.520
That day, l jumped in without thinking.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.860
l was simply determined to protect the girl in front of my eyes.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:39.460
<i>And that determination</i> <i>hasn't changed since.</i>

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:43.340
<i>lf anything, it has grown stronger.</i>

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.330
<i>l want to protect her!</i>

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.810
l've decided, Tokiko.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:55.940
But...

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.390
l am a bit lacking in courage.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:03.550
ls that so...

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:07.190
ln that case, l will make up for what you lack.

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:08.120
Right...!

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:12.520
lt's as l once said.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.590
The time when you die, is also the time when l die.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:21.140
You and l are as one mind and one body!

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.850
Staking your final hopes on one thing alone, the white kakugane,

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.230
you go to confront Victor...

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:54.690
But Kazuki, l will not let you go alone.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:58.630
Next time: "When You Die, I'll Die With You."

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:06.810
Mahiro Muto's Buso Renkin Seminar!

00:21:08.110 --> 00:21:09.980
Hello! This is Mahiro Muto!

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:12.250
And l'm here to introduce another Baboom...

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:14.410
Set of Buso Renkin!

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:15.920
Believe it or not,

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:20.020
for our eighth round it's the whole gang from the Alchemist Army!

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:23.060
First up is this guy, Genji lkusabe.

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:26.900
With a name difficult to read and sounding like a samurai,

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:32.200
Mr. lkusabe wields the Cross Spear Buso Renkin, "Gekisen."

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:35.530
lts special property is rapid regeneration.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.510
ln other words,

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:40.270
even if the spear and the wielder are damaged, whoosh!

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:43.610
lt will automatically repair itself in an instant!

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:46.620
Next is Shinobu Negoro!

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:52.490
Mr. Negoro wields the Ninja Sword
Buso Renkin "Secret Trail."

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.620
He says with this,

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:59.160
he can cut through objects to enter and exit subspace at will.

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:03.460
Coming out of the darkness in stealth...
Now that's a Ninja!

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:06.410
Uh... by the way, what's a subspace?

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:10.570
Urr... l mean, next we have Rintaro lnukai.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:13.280
Mr. lnukai's Buso Renkin is a Dog!

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:16.940
Well, not exactly, it's a military dog
Buso Renkin called "Killer Rabies."

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:19.450
But well, simply put, it's a Dog!

00:22:20.320 --> 00:22:27.730
A Dog-type robot that is way more amazing than a real dog.

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:32.130
But when it comes to real dogs,
Mr. lnukai is totally afraid of them.

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:34.230
That makes no sense...

00:22:34.730 --> 00:22:37.860
Oh, and next there's Madoka Maruyama.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.000
The name and appearance may sound and look like a woman,

00:22:41.070 --> 00:22:43.510
but he is a full fledged "Man"!

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:47.780
Mr. Maruyama uses a Floating Mine.

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:48.840
ln other words,

00:22:48.910 --> 00:22:51.350
an explosive balloon Buso Renkin called the "Bubble Cage."

00:22:51.420 --> 00:22:55.380
The creepy-faced balloons surround the target and explode,

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:59.150
the number of balloons increases and presses down on the target!

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:02.690
And then there's Hanaka Busujima.

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:05.730
She's REALLY so cute,

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:10.790
but thanks to that Bulky Gasmask
Buso Renkin "Aerial Operator,"

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:12.810
you can't see Hanaka-chan's true face.

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:16.170
With her Buso Renkin, she can mix and create all sorts of gas.

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:19.450
Hmm... But l still want to see her face!

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:24.510
And next, could it be Bravo's girlfriend?!

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:28.520
Or sort of, or maybe not, kind of person Chitose Tateyama.

00:23:28.990 --> 00:23:32.190
Ms. Chitose's Buso Renkin is the "Hermes Drive."

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:33.820
Taking the shape of a Radar,

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.730
it can locate anyone as long as you know them,

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:38.660
and furthermore allows her the ability of teleportation.

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:41.530
lt sure would be useful if you had one of these, wouldn't it?!

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:43.000
l want one too!

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:47.700
And then, and then, there's Warrior Chief Sekima Hiwatari.

00:23:47.770 --> 00:23:51.970
His Buso Renkin is a napalm bomb called "Blaze of Glory,"

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:55.140
capable of creating an instantaneous maximum temperature

00:23:55.210 --> 00:23:57.950
of 5100° C. (appx. 10,000° F) and burn away everything in it's path!

00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:01.720
Err...or so he says, but...5100 degrees?

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:04.890
Well, it must mean it's VERY hot, right?

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:06.850
And not just that!

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:08.660
There's his Pyro Fusion,

00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:13.430
where he can merge with that super hot flame to nullify the opponent's attacks.

00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:16.400
l'm saying all of this without really knowing too well!

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:21.270
And last, but not least!
Great Warrior Chief Shosei Sakaguchi!

00:24:21.340 --> 00:24:23.570
He sure doesn't go by the title of Great Warrior Chief for nothing,

00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:27.980
as his Buso Renkin is the Giant Robot "Buster Baron"!

00:24:28.050 --> 00:24:32.380
What part of that is a Buso Renkin, that's just way over the top!

00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:37.290
Plus, the Buster Baron can power up other people's Buso Renkin for it to use!

00:24:37.490 --> 00:24:42.020
And that's the Buso Renkin from all the Alchemist Army!

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.260
l'm tired.....

00:24:46.300 --> 00:24:50.240
And so next time... is our final sem.

00:24:50.300 --> 00:24:51.600
Please tune in, okay?

00:24:57.680 --> 00:25:01.200
Mahiro Illustration by Taeko Hori
